From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:07:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mkfs: give `getfullblkname()` a prototype

`mkfs.c` declares it in the K&R style:

    extern char	*getfullblkname();

Under C23 an empty parameter list means "takes no arguments" rather
than "unspecified", so the one call site becomes an error:

    mkfs.c:1428:27: error: too many arguments to function
        `getfullblkname`; expected 0, have 1

Spell out the parameter. This is what the neighbouring consumers of the
same libadm routine already do -- see `ufs/roll_log/roll_log.c` and
`udfs/mkfs/mkfs.c`, both of which declare `getfullblkname(char *)` --
so this brings `ufs/mkfs` in line with the rest of `cmd/fs.d` rather
than inventing anything.

`ufs/df`, `ufs/tunefs` and `udfs/fsck` still carry the K&R form and
will need the same treatment; they are left alone here because nothing
in this series builds them.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5)
---
 usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
index 94ed8b734f..515ad80100 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/ufs/mkfs/mkfs.c
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@
 #include	<sys/asynch.h>
 
 extern offset_t	llseek();
-extern char	*getfullblkname();
+extern char	*getfullblkname(char *);
 extern long	lrand48();
 
 extern int	optind;
